<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 14.59 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 14.59 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 14.59 percent at an auction on Tuesday from 17.23 percent at the last auction on May 13,  the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   May 20	     May 13</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K2108977     KZ43K1408972</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  650		  550</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 2,610		2,220</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 672		  601</p>
<p> Average price			 96.48 pct	  95.87 pct</p>
<p> Average yield			 14.59 pct	  17.23 pct</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Aug 21, 1997     Aug 14, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
